# The debug flavour, on top of ps3.config: the research drivers. Each is a module nothing loads by
# itself (modprobe by hand, root only), and the release kernel has none of them (K4, round 3):
# - ps3lv1call (ps3/0250): any lv1 hypercall for root, flash and storage regions included; the
#   ps3disk write guard (local/0045) can't stop what goes through it;
# - ps3physmem (ps3/0140): all of the partition's memory mapped into userspace;
# - ps3dispmgr (ps3/0080): /dev/ps3dispmngr, the raw dispatcher manager, which carries the update
#   manager. In the debug flavour only, for research sessions with the user present
#   (docs/OTHEROS-PATCHES.md); never autoloaded in a normal session.
# package.conf REQUIRE_SET_debug / REQUIRE_UNSET_release keep this split from drifting.
CONFIG_PS3_LV1CALL=m
CONFIG_PS3_PHYSMEM=m
CONFIG_PS3_DISP_MANAGER=m
